{#-
  The shell every page of the site is built into. A page supplies its own <main> and nothing else:
  the doctype, the head, the stylesheet links and the closing tags are written once, here.

  Front matter a page may set:
    title       the page's name. "interesting" is appended, so index.html leaves it out.
    description the <meta name='description'>, omitted when absent.
    stylesheet  a name in css/: "diary" links css/diary.css after the shared css/site.css, so the
                page's own rules win over the shared ones. Omit it for a page that needs none.
    inlineStyles
                write the styles into the page instead of linking them. Only error.html needs it:
                CloudFront returns that page for any 404, at whatever path was asked for, so a
                relative <link> next to it would be a guess.
    footer      the links the page ends with, as [href, text] pairs (see footer.njk).
    footerNote  an aside shown after those links.

  The analytics and consent line is written here rather than in every page, which is the whole
  point of a shared shell: the axiom is about the built site, so one line here carries it to all of
  them (see ANALYTICS_TAG and check_analytics in .github/scripts/make_interesting.py). The
  local-state line below it is there for the same reason, and carries the same kind of axiom
  (STATE_TAG and check_state). Both lines are written once, here, and neither may be dropped: the
  files behind them are fixed, and a built page without either line is refused.

  Links are relative, like every link in the site: it has no fixed domain and may be served under
  a sub-path, so "css/site.css" and not "/css/site.css".
-#}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang='en'>
<head>
  <meta charset='utf-8'>
  <meta name='viewport' content='width=device-width, initial-scale=1'>
  <title>{% if title %}{{ title }} · {% endif %}interesting</title>
{%- if description %}
  <meta name='description' content='{{ description }}'>
{%- endif %}
{%- if inlineStyles %}
  <style>{{ 'site' | css | safe }}{{ stylesheet | css | safe }}</style>
{%- else %}
  <link rel='stylesheet' href='css/site.css'>
{%- if stylesheet %}
  <link rel='stylesheet' href='css/{{ stylesheet }}.css'>
{%- endif %}
{%- endif %}
  <!-- Analytics and the cookie consent banner that gates it; see js/analytics.js. -->
  <script src='js/analytics.js' defer></script>
  <!-- The one local-state store every page reads and writes through, and its meta menu; see
       js/state.js. Not deferred: a page's own script runs before any deferred one does. -->
  <script src='js/state.js'></script>
</head>
<body>
  <header class='site-header'>
    <p class='site-header-title'>
      <a href='index.html'>interesting</a>
      <span>one sky, many instruments</span>
    </p>
    <nav class='site-header-nav' aria-label='Primary navigation'>
      <a href='index.html'{% if page and page.fileSlug == 'index' %} aria-current='page'{% endif %}>home</a>
      <a href='constellation-diary.html'{% if page and page.fileSlug == 'constellation-diary' %} aria-current='page'{% endif %}>diary</a>
      <a href='constellation-echo.html'{% if page and page.fileSlug == 'constellation-echo' %} aria-current='page'{% endif %}>echo</a>
      <a href='constellation-weather.html'{% if page and page.fileSlug == 'constellation-weather' %} aria-current='page'{% endif %}>weather</a>
      <a href='orbital-weaver.html'{% if page and page.fileSlug == 'orbital-weaver' %} aria-current='page'{% endif %}>weaver</a>
      <a href='sky-archive.html'{% if page and page.fileSlug == 'sky-archive' %} aria-current='page'{% endif %}>archive</a>
      <a href='star-lantern.html'{% if page and page.fileSlug == 'star-lantern' %} aria-current='page'{% endif %}>lantern</a>
      <a href='wish-terrarium.html'{% if page and page.fileSlug == 'wish-terrarium' %} aria-current='page'{% endif %}>terrarium</a>
      <a href='sitemap.html'{% if page and page.fileSlug == 'sitemap' %} aria-current='page'{% endif %}>site map</a>
      <a href='sky-atlas.html'{% if page and page.fileSlug == 'sky-atlas' %} aria-current='page'{% endif %}>atlas alias</a>
      <a href='error.html'{% if page and page.fileSlug == 'error' %} aria-current='page'{% endif %}>404</a>
    </nav>
  </header>
{{ content | safe }}</body>
</html>
